# Skill Secondary Repos

Every skill under `.cursor/skills/` has its own standalone GitHub repo in the `responsum-team` org, authenticated via `PAT2`.

**When a skill file is modified, push to both:**
1. `elixirrjob1/cursorskills` (main repo) — `git push origin main`
2. The skill's own secondary repo — rsync + push (see sync method below)

## Sync method

```bash
source .env

SKILL=<skill-folder-name>   # e.g. dbt-model-from-stm
REPO=<repo-name>             # look up in table below

rm -rf /tmp/skill-sync-target
git clone "https://${PAT2_USER}:${PAT2}@github.com/responsum-team/${REPO}.git" /tmp/skill-sync-target
rsync -av --exclude='.git' .cursor/skills/${SKILL}/ /tmp/skill-sync-target/
cd /tmp/skill-sync-target
git add -A
git diff --cached --quiet || git commit -m "sync: update from elixirrjob1/cursorskills main"
git push
```

